      "writtenOn": "2019-10-07T15:37:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ideally it should be just an ordinary module that doesn\u0027t need to be unique, shouldn\u0027t it?\n\nI had a look into why it is this way, and iiuc the reason is that it eventually queries some product variables ([1] -\u003e [2]). If so, this could be made an ordinary module by either adding properties to specify which variables to query, or even better do away with them completely and specify the jars directly in dex_bootjars{} in the bp file.\n\nI\u0027m not suggesting that for this CL; it\u0027d be a fairly sizeable refactoring. Just mentioning it for checking my understanding, and if so phrase this differently.\n\n[1] https://devops-console-stagingoss.corp.google.com/android/platform/build/soong/+/3776d9546a60937c06dcab380aadd38b787b18e7:java/dexpreopt_config.go;l\u003d110-127;drc\u003d402be41aa8df98733a16eb8f96dd769dbe8c5d80\n[2] https://devops-console-stagingoss.corp.google.com/android/platform/build/+/8ca4bf76d682bfc87028c0acff24ca0388e87205:core/dex_preopt_config.mk;l\u003d101-103;drc\u003db324175118f50a1acfb40916215ad5f444338265",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 61,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "ab06fcaff184eb3a3c73d53cb4949dfa1fba221d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
