      "writtenOn": "2019-10-17T16:46:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Martin:\n\nI think the reason for singleton is not querying product variables (dexpreoptGlobalConfig can also be called with any context that provides the same context.Config(), and in my CL I pass a module context).\n\nI think the real reason is make variables generation that for a singleton is instance-specific (MakeVars method), but for a module is not (so the generation function cannot access the list of filenames in a particular module).\n\nFor now I think it is better to keep a singleton than to modify Soong to allow module-specific Make varaible generation (the modification is not difficult, but the new method would add confusion).\n\n\nColin:\n\nI tried ctx.Config().Once() locally, but the code became even more confusing:\n- First, there is no context available in a module constructor (factory), so I had to put it into GenerateAndroidBuildActions, which is rather late (I could use other visitors as well).\n- Second, when searching for unique module it is still necessary to handle \"improbable\" cases, because the check is in different file and has no apparent connection to the search (and the check does not ensure that the module exists at all).\n- Finally, in future we will likely need multiple dex_bootjars modules (for boot image extensions), so the check will go away in any case.",
      "parentUuid": "50442c62_5a5f211d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 61,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "ab06fcaff184eb3a3c73d53cb4949dfa1fba221d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
